; SELinux labelling for ownfs mounts.
;
; ownfs ignores the drive's stored ownership, and its labels describe the
; policy of whatever machine wrote them, so it is labelled like other
; removable media without usable labels (vfat, exfat, ntfs3): every file is
; dosfs_t, which desktop applications may read and write.
(genfscon ownfs "/" (system_u object_r dosfs_t ((s0) (s0))))
